  "items": [
    {
      "name": "Why the Itch and Flakes",
      "char_file": "단과자빵_illust.jpg",
      "body": ["A yeast called Malassezia", "lives on your scalp's oil", "", "It breaks down sebum into", "oleic acid, which irritates", "sensitive skin"]
    },
    {
      "name": "Sweets",
      "char_file": "단과자빵_illust.jpg",
      "body": ["Donuts and cookies spike", "blood sugar fast", "", "That raises insulin and IGF-1,", "a hormone that tells oil glands", "to make more sebum"]
    },
    {
      "name": "Instead of Sweets",
      "char_file": "단과자빵_illust.jpg",
      "body": ["Reach for berries or", "a handful of nuts instead"]
    },
    {
      "name": "Dairy",
      "char_file": "우유_illust.jpg",
      "body": ["Whole milk and ice cream", "were among the foods most", "linked to flare-ups", "in one clinical study", "", "Hormones in milk may push", "oil glands into overdrive"]
    },
    {
      "name": "Instead of Dairy",
      "char_file": "우유_illust.jpg",
      "body": ["Swap in unsweetened", "soy milk instead"]
    },
    {
      "name": "Fried Food",
      "char_file": "돼지껍질튀김_illust.jpg",
      "body": ["French fries and fried chicken", "use oils heavy in omega-6 fats", "", "That may drive inflammation", "and shift your sebum's makeup"]
    },
    {
      "name": "Instead of Fried",
      "char_file": "돼지껍질튀김_illust.jpg",
      "body": ["Try oven-roasted potatoes", "or grilled chicken breast"]
    }
  ],
  "closing": {
    "headline": [["Sweets, dairy, and fried food -", "you don't have to cut them out completely"], ["Cutting back and swapping in", "can ease scalp irritation"]],
